ld be inclined to  potentially make a formal claim of  misconduct against antonio brown that's  when it becomes a problem that's when  you have enough if you're the patriots  it's more than than just saying well we  can't fire the guy based on a civil  lawsuit now you've got  this smoking gun  of intimidation and harassment and look  there's other stuff out there we may not  know about i've said all week 10 hours  brittany taylor with the nfl what did  she say how persuasive was she how much  of that did the patriots know about what  kind of investigation have the patriots  been doing on their own if if i'm robert  kraft i want to know  what i'm dealing with i want to know who  this guy is he's been accused in a civil  action that's not enough to take action  against him but it's enough to put me on  notice that i should use some of my  resources to figure out exactly who i'm  dealing with because if this goes  sideways it's going to reflect poorly on  the patriots and yes they're at a point  now where they may have to write off  nine million dollars but the nine  million dollars that they give up in  moving on from antonio brown could pale  in comparison to the damage that keeping  him could do to their brand  so  look it's now uh 1006 a.m eastern as i  say these words i won't be surprised if  he's on the commissioner exemplist by  the end of the day and i won't be  surprised if the patriots cut him by the  end of the day that's how alarming these  intimidating and harassing text messages  are to me we'll see if the patriots  agree we'll see if the league agrees and  we'll see you next week for pft live and  pft ot enjoy the week three games and  we'll talk to you soon
 

